<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νουμην-ία</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Att.
		
		
			contr.
		 for <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεομηνία</span></b>  (which
		occurs in <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			4.35
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			6.57
		</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
			<u>PMag.Leid.W.</u>
			1.28
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			9.43
		</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			14.298
		</span></i>):—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νευμηνία</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			1106.19
		</span></i> (Cos, <span class="entity">iv/iii B.C.</span>) ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεμονηΐα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>GDI</u>
			5015.28
		</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">Crete</span>) ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομενία</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
			167.5
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>new moon : the first of the month,</i> Pi.l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				<u>Fr.</u>
				58
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ach.</u>
				999
			</span></i> (pl.), etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. κατὰ
			σελήνην</span> to denote the <i>true</i> or <i>natural new
				moon,</i> as opp. to the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νουμηνία</span> of the calendars, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.28
			</span></i> ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κατὰ θεὸν ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMag.Par.</u>
					1.787
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2389
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. τοῦ ἔτους,</span> of the
			spring equinox, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				91
			</span></i>.</div>
